        heading: "Milking Parlor Washdown Design Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before the washdown plumbing design is finalized:\n\n• Hot-water budget built from CIP cycles, hose use, and sinks, checked against winter groundwater temperatures\n• Heater storage sized for back-to-back CIP cycles at shift changes\n• Heat recovery from milk refrigeration preheating the cold-water feed\n• Corrosion-resistant piping, gaskets, and hangers rated for chlorinated alkaline and acid cleaners\n• Hose stations covering the pit, holding pen, and return lanes, each with backflow protection\n• Recirculated or heat-traced hot-water distribution so far stations get hot water fast\n• Freeze protection on exterior hose stations and piping in cold climates\n• Floor slopes and trench drains sized for the washdown peak, with sediment handling for sand and solids",
