        question: "Do biofilters really work on barn exhaust?",
        answer: "Yes, when they're engineered rather than improvised. A properly sized biofilter — right media, right contact time, even air distribution, maintained moisture — removes a large fraction of the odorous compounds from ventilated exhaust. The failures are all design or maintenance failures: undersized beds, channeling from poor distribution, dried-out media. The engineer sizes the bed honestly for the airflow and includes the monitoring that keeps the biology alive.",
