        question: "What velocity does a CIP wash need in the milk line?",
        answer: "Typically around 5 feet per second — fast enough to scour milk soil mechanically, not just soak it. The engineer sizes the CIP supply pump to deliver that velocity through the longest circuit at the design head, because velocity at the pump means nothing if friction in a long parlor run drops it at the far end. Temperature and contact time complete the protocol: hot enough, long enough, and fast enough, all three.",
